ructions by the director.\\n- Make the ad design, layout, typography on-branded, but should look premium, editorial-like.\\n- Establish a clear visual hierarchy: one dominant focal point the eye lands on\\n  first, then the supporting message, then the CTA.\\n- Keep strong figure/ground contrast. If text sits over imagery, place a scrim or\\n  overlay behind it so it stays fully legible.\\n- Place the focal subject on a rule-of-thirds line; leave generous whitespace and\\n  avoid clutter.\\n- Use a limited palette anchored to the brand colors (~60-30-10), reserving one\\n  accent color for the call to action.\\n- Keep 20% space all around the creative for the ad to look cleaner\\n- Group and align elements cleanly (Gestalt); use at most two type styles.\",\"source\":\"campaign-creatives\",\"language\":\"English\",\"lastError\":null,\"imageModel\":\"openai/gpt-image-2:100\",\"hasNSFWRisk\":false,\"imagePrompt\":\"Instructions by the director: Using the PAS framework to target top of funnel discovery, this static 1:1 ad addresses the Problem Solver archetype by dramatizing the daily friction of tired, dehydrated skin. The visual hero is a bold, split-screen graphic: the left side is a muted, desaturated Mist Gray (#f2f4f7) representing dull, lifeless skin texture, while the right side is a high-energy, vibrant coral-pink splash of the dissolved collagen drink next to the clean white 'glow' tub, representing instant revival. The high-impact on-image headline is written in clean, medium-weight Circular Std and reads: 'Tired of dull morning skin?' A pill-shaped accent tag at the top in Primary Brand Orange (#ff5000) highlights 'Korean Marine Collagen.' The soft call to action at the bottom reads 'See how it works.' Keep this creative on-brand by pairing the clinical Mist Gray with the vibrant action orange gradient, utilizing sharp miter-stroke icons to signal scientific validation, and ensuring the product packaging is shown clearly at the center of the color transition