 text \\\"WELLBEING NUTRITION\\\" surrounding a stylized central letter \\\"W\\\" with a single tiny green leaf on its top-right tip. Below the logo is a large, rectangular framed section in a deeper coral shade that houses the product name \\\"glow\\\" stacked above \\\"collagen^\\\" in a prominent, elegant white serif lowercase font, directly followed by black Korean characters \\\"글로우 콜라겐\\\" and black descriptive text specifying \\\"Korean Marine Collagen Peptides with Liposomal Glutathione, Vitamin C, Resveratrol and DigeZyme®,\\\" alongside \\\"Type I & III\\\" and a white horizontal banner highlighting \\\"Tropical Bliss Flavour.\\\" To the right of this frame sits a circular graphic featuring a pink-and-white geodesic, triangular grid pattern bordered by the curved text \\\"Wild Caught • Mercury Free,\\\" with a small red \\\"Clinically Approved\\\" cross seal above it. The bottom edge of the label displays five small black line-art skin-benefit icons lined up horizontally above text indicating a net weight of 250g. When the dry powder product inside is mixed with water as directed, it dissolves to form a vibrant, translucent coral-pink beverage.\\n\\nUse the product appearance text only as a private visual reference for accurately drawing the product. Do not print, quote, paraphrase, label, or turn any of that description into ad copy. Treat orientation-specific details carefully: show front-only details only when the product front is visible; if the brief shows the back, side, top, or an angled view where those details would not be visible, omit them instead of moving them onto the wrong face.\\n\\nThe attached product photos show the real product — reproduce it faithfully.\\n\\nDesign requirements (apply to this ad):\\n- Follow the instructions by the director.\\n- Make the ad design, layout, typography on-branded, but should look premium, editorial-like.\\n- Establish a clear visual hierarchy: one dominant focal point the eye lands on\\n  first, then the